@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+## Why
+
+A customer placed an order with a single-use welcome code, cancelled it, and was refused the code on the corrected order ("already used"). The README says cancelling gives the coupon back. Cancelling currently hands the coupon back under the customer's name instead of the order's id, so the release never matches and the coupon stays used.
+
+The second report (free shipping at exactly €50.00) was investigated: `shippingCost` already treats 5000 cents as free, and the `shipping` spec and a test cover it (fixed earlier). It is not changed here beyond a regression test through the order path.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Cancelling an order gives back its single-use coupon, identified by the order that used it.
+- Add regression tests: place, cancel, re-place with a single-use coupon; and an order whose goods come to exactly 5000 cents ships free.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `coupons`: adds the single-use rule (one order only; given back on cancellation).
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/orders.ts` (`cancel`), tests in `test/`.
